## Final answer of writer
## Summary

I successfully fixed the bug where paging was skipping the last item. The issue was in the `paginate` function in `src/paging.js`:

**Problem**: Using `Math.floor(items.length / size)` meant that when there were leftover items that didn't fill a complete page, they were ignored.

**Solution**: Changed `Math.floor(items.length / size)` to `Math.ceil(items.length / size)` to ensure all items are included, even if the last page isn't full.

**Verification**: All tests now pass, including the test case that was failing: `paginate([1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 2)` now correctly returns `[[1, 2], [3, 4], [5]]` instead of skipping the last item `[5]`.

The fix is minimal, targeted, and handles all edge cases correctly including empty arrays, single items, and cases where the page size is larger than the number of items.

